# Walkthrough – Student Report System Upgrade

## What Was Built

Upgraded the existing student report system from static if-else logic to a CMS-ready module with **ML-based grading**, **3 certificate types**, and **role-based access functions**.

### New/Modified Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [data_loader.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/data_loader.py) | Loads Excel data, validates marks, supports teacher overrides |
| [model.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/model.py) | Random Forest ML model (replaces all if-else grading) |
| [report_generator.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/report_generator.py) | PDF report cards using ML output |
| [certificate_generator.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/certificate_generator.py) | 3 certificate types: Academic, Behavior, Punctuality |
| [cms_integration.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/cms_integration.py) | CMS API functions for student/teacher/admin roles |
| [main.py](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/main.py) | Updated entry point running full pipeline |
| [requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/requirements.txt) | Added scikit-learn, joblib |

### Key Design Decisions

- **ML Model**: Random Forest trained on 2000 synthetic samples, saved via joblib to [models/grade_model.pkl](file:///c:/Users/user/Documents/student_report_system/models/grade_model.pkl)
- **Excel Format**: Uses the user's updated 80-student file with all subjects out of 100 and Obedient/Punctual out of 10
- **Certificates**: Landscape PDFs with gold borders, corner decorations, signature placeholders
- **CMS Module**: Pure Python functions (no framework dependency) — ready to import into Django/Flask CMS

---

## Verification Results

### Pipeline Run
- ✅ `python main.py` — exit code 0
- ✅ 80 report cards generated in `media/reports/`
- ✅ 53 certificates generated in `media/certificates/` (35 punctuality, 18 behavior)
- ✅ No academic excellence certs (expected — no student has ≥90% in ALL 9 subjects)

### ML Model
- ✅ Predicts correct grade (A+ for ~95% student), proper remarks, and full badge set
- ✅ Model persists to `models/grade_model.pkl` and loads on subsequent runs

### CMS Functions
- ✅ `get_student_access(201)` returns report path + certificate paths
- ✅ `get_teacher_access([201, 202])` returns docs for multiple students
- ✅ `update_student_marks(201, {"Maths": 95, "English": 88})` regenerates report with updated marks

### File Integrity
- ✅ Report PDFs ~435KB (includes badge images)
- ✅ Certificate PDFs ~2.8KB (text-only professional layout)

---

## CMS Integration Reference

```python
# Student role
from cms_integration import get_student_access
docs = get_student_access(201)  # returns {report, certificates}

# Teacher role
from cms_integration import update_student_marks, get_teacher_access
update_student_marks(201, {"Maths": 95})  # edit + regenerate
docs = get_teacher_access([201, 202, 203])  # view assigned students

# Admin role
from cms_integration import get_admin_access, generate_all_reports
generate_all_reports()           # regenerate everything
all_docs = get_admin_access()    # access all students
```
